-- title:
--   Rank comparison of localised Hecke algebras via extension of lifts
-- statement:
--   Fix an integer $N \neq 0$ and sets of naturals $S_0 \subseteq S$ such that every prime divisor of $N$ lies in $S$, and let $\mathcal{O}$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, adically complete for its maximal ideal and with finite residue field. Assume [`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L6), i.e. the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathbb{Z}$-span of those weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are integers is the whole space. For a set $T$ of naturals, [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 T`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) is the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin T$ together with the $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin T$; thus $S_0 \subseteq S$ gives an inclusion of `heckeAlgebra N 2 S` into `heckeAlgebra N 2 S₀`. Given ring homomorphisms $\theta$ from `heckeAlgebra N 2 S` and $\theta'$ from `heckeAlgebra N 2 S₀` to the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$, assume: for every characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation domain $\mathcal{O}'$ with finite residue field which is a module-finite $\mathcal{O}$-algebra along an injective local structure map, and every ring homomorphism $\chi$ from `heckeAlgebra N 2 S` to $\mathcal{O}'$ whose reduction is $\theta$ read in the residue field of $\mathcal{O}'$, there is a further such $\mathcal{O}''$, module-finite over $\mathcal{O}'$ along an injective local structure map, and a ring homomorphism $\chi'$ from `heckeAlgebra N 2 S₀` to $\mathcal{O}''$ which restricts along the inclusion to $\chi$ composed with $\mathcal{O}' \to \mathcal{O}''$ and whose reduction is $\theta'$ read in the residue field of $\mathcal{O}''$. Then the $\mathcal{O}$-rank of [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131), the localisation of `heckeBaseAlgebra N S 𝒪` at the image under `latticeBaseChange` of the complement of the prime `heckeCharKernel N S 𝒪 θ`, is at most the $\mathcal{O}$-rank of [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S₀ 𝒪 θ'`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131).
--
--   This is the commutative-algebra half of the comparison between the Hecke algebra away from $S$ and the fuller algebra away from $S_0$, localised at the maximal ideals cut out by $\theta$ and $\theta'$: the arithmetic input is packaged as the hypothesis that every characteristic-zero lift of the residual eigensystem $\theta$ extends, after a finite local extension of the coefficient ring, to a lift of $\theta'$. It feeds the bijectivity and rank statements [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.bijective_of_subset_of_forall_prime_mem_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.bijective_of_subset_of_forall_prime_mem_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq) and [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.finrank_le_of_subset_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.finrank_le_of_subset_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq).
-- source:
